### A1 Height channel and how Painter combines height with normal (11 October 2026)

- Sources: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/painting/advanced-channel-painting/height-map-painting , https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/interface/texture-set/texture-set-settings , https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/painting/advanced-channel-painting/normal-map-painting , https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/interface/layer-stack/blending-modes , https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/compare-mask (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: the Height channel is stored in a high dynamic range format, so it keeps negative and positive values and is not capped at the 0 to 255 ceiling of classic height maps (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: a bitmap or procedural source painted into Height is remapped from its 0 to 255 range to -1 to +1, so mid-gray means zero; darker values subtract height and lighter values add height under the default blend mode, Linear Dodge (Add); a flat color lets you type an exact height between -1 and 1 (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: Painter composites the painted height through all layers, converts it to a normal in real time and blends it with the baked high-poly normal, so a high-poly detail normal plus a painted height is enough (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: in Solo view the default preview shows only positive values and shows negative values as strong black; a plus/minus display mode shows both signs and a Scale setting widens the visible range (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: Texture Set setting "Normal mixing" is Combine by default (a detail-oriented function merges the Normal channel with the baked normal) or Replace (only the Normal and Height channels build the final normal and the baked normal disappears from the viewport) (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: Texture Set setting "Height to normal method" is Smooth (Sobel), the default, which gives a smoother normal that may lose fine detail, or Sharp, which is crisper with a risk of noise and aliasing and suits repeating patterns such as fabric (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: Texture Set setting "Ambient occlusion mixing" is Replace or Multiply (default); "UV padding" is 3D Space Neighbor (default) or 2D Space Neighbor and the Normal channel always uses the 2D method; channel storage formats are 8-bit, 16-bit and 16/32-bit float; internal channels are capped at 4096 and exports go up to 8192 when the GPU supports it (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: the Normal channel has three layer blend modes only for normals: Normal Map Combine (Whiteout style), Normal Map Detail (reoriented, keeps flat areas and both strengths) and Normal Map Inverse Detail (the bottom normal is reoriented to the top surface); painting normals defaults to Detail (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: right-click "Add mask with height combination" adds a Compare Mask effect and sets the Height channel blend mode to Normal; Compare Mask compares a chosen channel of a source side and a target side (layers below, this layer, this mask, or a constant) with an operation of lower than, within tolerance or higher than, a Hardness control and a Histogram view (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: the Height To Normal filter has Overwrite Existing Normal, Use World Units, Normal Intensity (only when world units are off), Surface Size in cm and Height Depth in cm (only when world units are on); no normal orientation or blend option is listed on its page (11 October 2026)
- COP: height is a Mono layer (floating point); keep detail layers zero-mean so that `blend` Add behaves like Painter Linear Dodge on signed values (LOCAL: Copernicus1.md line 1627 states that every detail layer must have a zero mean) (11 October 2026)
