### A2 Baked mesh maps (bakers) and what each is used for (11 October 2026)

Baking mode (shortcut F8) produces the mesh maps that generators, filters, smart materials and smart masks read; the same ideas exist in Copernicus as the outputs of `bakegeometrytextures` (version 2.0 in Houdini 22) with `bakepreprocess` as the new ray set-up node. (11 October 2026)

#### A2.1 Normal map from mesh (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/normal-map-from-mesh (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: moves the detail of a high-poly mesh onto the low-poly mesh as a normal map; Painter always bakes tangent space and follows the project orientation (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: Map Type (world or tangent, hidden in Painter), Normal Orientation (OpenGL or DirectX, DirectX is the baker default, tangent space only) (11 October 2026)
- Height role (UNVERIFIED reading): it is the base normal into which painted height is mixed when Normal mixing is Combine, so it carries the large relief that Height then refines (11 October 2026)
- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` outputs `normal` (tangent) and `edgenormal` (rounded edges without extra geometry); Normal Space and Normal Y Direction choose signed or offset and the Y orientation; no bake is needed for a flat texture, use `heighttonormal` (11 October 2026)

#### A2.2 World space normals (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/world-space-normals (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: stores normal, tangent or binormal in world space, which lets generators find surfaces that face up, down or sideways (dust on upward faces) (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: Baking Type (Normal default, Tangent, Binormal), optional Normal Map input, Normal Orientation (OpenGL or DirectX, DirectX default, Normal type only) (11 October 2026)
- Height role (UNVERIFIED reading): indirect, it decides where height-like deposits such as dust or snow are allowed (11 October 2026)
- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `worldnormal`; for a flat tile UNVERIFIED: `heighttonormal` with Normal Type Signed then `channelsplit` to isolate the component that says "facing up" (11 October 2026)

#### A2.3 ID (Color Map from Mesh) (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/color-map-from-mesh and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: bakes a distinct color per part of the mesh so selections and masks are easy (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: Color Source (Vertex Color blended smoothly between vertices, Material Color per face, Mesh ID per object, Polygroup or Submesh ID per element; the Painter page also names file ID), Color Generator (Random, Hue Shift or Grayscale, only for the ID sources) (11 October 2026)
- Height role (UNVERIFIED reading): per-part masks that include or exclude a height treatment such as wear (11 October 2026)
- COP: `idtomask` (ID Pattern, Keep by Range, Keep by Chance with Probability and Seed, Keep within Mask), `idtomono` (Conversion Cast, Safe Pack or Bitwise) and `monotoid` convert ids; the `custom` output of `bakegeometrytextures` rasterizes user attributes (UNVERIFIED that an id attribute travels through it); flat substitutes are `segmentbyconnectivity` id, `cellularnoise` id and `tilepattern` id (11 October 2026)

#### A2.4 Ambient occlusion (11 October 2026)
- Sources: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/ambient-occlusion and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings (11 October 2026)
