#### T01 Height first, separate reads, value-range hygiene (11 October 2026)
- Problem solved (author summary, UNVERIFIED): detail built before the large forms makes the silhouette unreadable and forces rework; a narrow or clipped value range makes later blends peak or flatten (11 October 2026)
- Designer chain (SOURCE): reference first; large shapes, then mid breakups, then micro detail; judge height together with Normal and AO from the first nodes; keep a wide range without pure black or white and use Auto Levels to restore it; stack heights with Max Lighten; compress the base into 0 to 0.8 to leave 0.8 to 1 for surface detail (azulejos); keep grunge out of the early stage (Perez); keep node count low (Charlie Foreman); expose few parameters (Perez, Lynch) (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus chain: one named block per read (macro, meso, micro) each ending in a `null`, merged with `blend` (Maximum for raised unions, Add for zero-mean sculpting deltas, Mask = amplitude); monitors kept beside the chain: `heighttonormal`, `heighttoambientocclusion`, `curvature`; range tools: Auto Levels node = `equalize` (OFFICIAL-MAP), Levels node = `remap` (OFFICIAL-MAP); the headroom compression is `remap` Output Min 0 and Output Max 0.8 (UNVERIFIED mapping) (11 October 2026)
- Parameter hints: the `equalize` page warns that equalizing per frame can flicker for procedural changes and recommends a `remap` with a fixed range; `remap` Compute Range fills Input Min and Max from the layer; `statistics` outputs average, minimum and maximum (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/equalize.html and https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/statistics.html) (11 October 2026)
- Additional documented practice (SOURCE, Stan Brown and Margot Casiro in B3.11 and B3.12): start the height from a mid-gray base (0.5 in 16-bit) so values add or subtract, narrow the value range of each layer so layers combine without clamping, read the histogram while building, run an autolevels pass at the end and finish height before any dependent map is built; COP form, UNVERIFIED: `constant` for the 0.5 base, `blend` Add or Maximum per layer, `equalize` or a fixed `remap` last, `statistics` to read minimum and maximum (11 October 2026)
- Visual signature (UNVERIFIED): the reference shows readable large masses at thumbnail size, mid-size steps at half size and tooth only at full size; if tooth is the only readable scale the surface is micro-only (fabric, sandpaper) and the macro block can stay flat (11 October 2026)
- Local notes: Copernicus1.md line 1537 imposes node names of the form letter, number, subject, role (for example `C03_TL__distance_to_corner`) and line 1627 requires every detail layer to have a zero mean; line 1509 records that an earlier fiber-wood attempt failed partly because the macro form came after the fibers (11 October 2026)

#### T02 Shape blockout, bevel profiles and distance fields (11 October 2026)
- Problem solved (author summary, UNVERIFIED): give each tile, stone or cell a believable footprint and cross-section (flat top, bevel, dish, pillow) before any damage (11 October 2026)
- Designer chain (SOURCE): Tile Generator for grids; polygon plus linear gradient in minimum-darken into Tile Random (Soto); primitives combined by add and subtract, blurred, histogram-scanned and warped (Caggese); Edge Detect plus Bevel for tile seams (Prakapenka); Edge Detect to bevel corners, Distance to clear small bubbles and Transformation 2D doubling resolution during the bevel (paver); warped Cells 4 for irregular facets (Goodbrand); the Distance node grows masks more predictably than blur and bevels with a sharp linear falloff, with Euclidean, Manhattan or Chebyshev metrics (https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/distance) (11 October 2026)
